Your task is to complete the implementation of the file system traversal algorithm using a stack-based approach, ensuring that it correctly traverses the file system and returns the IDs of the resources encountered in a depth-first manner.

Implement the `FileSystemTraversal` struct with the following methods:
- `new(root: DirOrResource) -> Self`: Creates a new instance of `FileSystemTraversal` with the root directory or resource.
- `next(&mut self) -> Option<ResourceId>`: Returns the next resource ID encountered during traversal, or `None` if traversal is complete.

You should use the provided code snippet as a starting point and build upon it to complete the file system traversal algorithm.

```rust
// Given enum representing a directory or a resource
enum DirOrResource {
    Dir { name: String, iter: Vec<DirOrResource> },
    Resource(ResourceId),
}

// Given resource ID type
type ResourceId = u64;

// Implement the file system traversal algorithm using a stack
struct FileSystemTraversal {
    stack: Vec<DirOrResource>,
}

impl FileSystemTraversal {
    fn new(root: DirOrResource) -> Self {
        let mut stack = Vec::new();
        stack.push(root);
        FileSystemTraversal { stack }
    }

    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<ResourceId> {
        while let Some(node) = self.stack.pop() {
            match node {
                DirOrResource::Dir { name, iter } => {
                    for item in iter.into_iter().rev() {
                        self.stack.push(item);
                    }
                }
                DirOrResource::Resource(id) => return Some(id),
            }
        }
        None
    }
}
```

