The `unsafe_global_var!` macro is used to declare a mutable static variable `KMSG` of type `KmsgSection`, which represents the section of memory for storing kernel messages. The `safe_global_var!` macro is used to declare a static variable `BUFFER_INDEX` of type `AtomicUsize`, which will be used to keep track of the buffer index for thread-safe operations.

Your task is to implement the `KmsgSection` struct and the circular buffer operations `push_message` and `pop_message` in a thread-safe manner using the provided `KMSG` and `BUFFER_INDEX` variables.

```rust
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::sync::{Mutex, MutexGuard};

const KMSG_SIZE: usize = 100;

struct KmsgSection {
    buffer: [u8; KMSG_SIZE + 1],
}

static mut KMSG: KmsgSection = KmsgSection {
    buffer: [0; KMSG_SIZE + 1],
};

static BUFFER_INDEX: AtomicUsize = AtomicUsize::new(0);

fn push_message(msg: &str) {
    let mut index = BUFFER_INDEX.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
    let msg_bytes = msg.as_bytes();
    let mut kmsg = unsafe { &mut KMSG.buffer };

    for &byte in msg_bytes {
        kmsg[index] = byte;
        index = (index + 1) % KMSG_SIZE;
    }

    BUFFER_INDEX.store(index, Ordering::Relaxed);
}

fn pop_message() -> Option<String> {
    let index = BUFFER_INDEX.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
    let kmsg = unsafe { &KMSG.buffer };

    if index == 0 {
        return None;
    }

    let mut message = Vec::new();
    let mut i = index;

    while kmsg[i] != 0 && i != 0 {
        message.push(kmsg[i]);
        i = (i + 1) % KMSG_SIZE;
    }

    let message_str = String::from_utf8_lossy(&message).into_owned();
    BUFFER_INDEX.store(i, Ordering::Relaxed);
    Some(message_str)
}
```

