In the solution, the `new` method takes ownership of the initial value and returns a new `BufferSet` instance. The `get` method returns a reference to the inner data without allowing mutation, while the `get_mut` method returns a mutable reference to the inner data, allowing mutation. The `Spinlock` is used to provide thread-safe access to the inner data of the buffer set.

