fn count_divisors_optimized(n: u32) -> u32 {
    let mut count = 0;
    let mut i = 1;
    while i * i <= n {
        if n % i == 0 {
            // If divisors are equal, count only one
            if n / i == i {
                count += 1;
            } else {
                count += 2;
            }
        }
        i += 1;
    }
    count
}

fn main() {
    // Test cases
    assert_eq!(count_divisors_optimized(6), 4); // 1, 2, 3, 6
    assert_eq!(count_divisors_optimized(10), 4); // 1, 2, 5, 10
    assert_eq!(count_divisors_optimized(25), 3); // 1, 5, 25
}
```

The `count_divisors_optimized` function efficiently counts the divisors of the given positive integer `n` by iterating up to the square root of `n` and counting the divisors based on the remainder of the division. The time complexity of this solution is O(sqrt(n)), making it more efficient than the brute force approach.

